Third-party material included in this folder
--------------------------------------------

* SkyWater SKY130 open PDK (Apache License 2.0). Derived from it: the
  layout-extracted standard-cell netlists in data/pdk/pex/, the routed layouts in
  data/layout/ (DEF files, and one GDS file that contains SKY130 standard-cell
  geometry), and the calibration data in data/pdk/sky130_*/ and glitchscope/data/.

* GlobalFoundries GF180MCU open PDK (Apache License 2.0). Derived from it: the
  calibration data in data/pdk/gf180mcu_7t_3v3/ and
  glitchscope/data/gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__tt_025C_3v30/.

* bench/netlists/c17.v is a synthesised version of the ISCAS-85 benchmark c17,
  as distributed by ISPRAS hdl-benchmarks (Apache License 2.0).

* The gate-level netlists in build_pdk/ were synthesised by GlitchScope's own
  generator against the cell libraries of SKY130, GF180MCU, IHP SG13G2,
  Nangate45, ASAP7 and GT2N as distributed with OpenROAD-flow-scripts. They
  contain cell names only, no library data.


Third-party material used but not included
------------------------------------------

* Benchmark circuits are downloaded at pinned commits by bench/fetch_benchmarks.py
  (ISCAS-85/89 via ISPRAS hdl-benchmarks, Apache License 2.0; EPFL suite, MIT;
  ITC'99 via PoliTo I99T, EUPL-1.2) and the PicoRV32 core by
  bench/picorv32/fetch.sh (ISC licence). Only results derived from them are
  included.

* GLOW (ETH Zurich) is run from its own checkout, which needs a Gurobi licence.
  Only its results are included; neither is needed to run the notebook.

* The open-source tools used to produce the data (Yosys, ABC, Icarus Verilog,
  ngspice, OpenROAD, OpenROAD-flow-scripts, OpenSTA, Magic, KLayout, HiGHS) are
  not included.
